# Shell scripts must stay LF regardless of the committer's platform — a
# stray \r in the shebang line breaks the interpreter lookup on Linux
# ("/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory"), and this repo is
# edited on Windows but deployed to Linux (see docs/deploy-proxmox.md).
*.sh text eol=lf

# YAML is more tolerant of CRLF than a shebang line, but GitHub Actions
# workflows are executed on Linux runners — keep them LF for the same
# cross-platform reason, not because a real failure was observed.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
